   1 #!/usr/bin/env python3
   2 """#457: a guest UTLB associative write matching two entries ended the host.
   3 
   4 Prints one line per row:  <name> <got> <want> ok|FAIL
   5 then SH_TLBMULTI_CONTROL=OK|DEAD and SH_TLBMULTI_RESULT=<passed>/<total>.
   6 gate_sh_rounding.sh does the asserting.
   7 
   8 What this protects
   9 ------------------
  10 `dev_sh4.c` raises `sh_exception(cpu, EXPEVT_RESET_TLB_MULTI_HIT, 0, 0)` when an
  11 ASSOCIATIVE write to the UTLB address array matches more than one entry.
  12 `sh_exception()` had no case for `0x140`, so it fell to the `default:` arm and ran
  13 `exit(1)`.  Three ordinary privileged guest stores ended the host process.
  14 
  15 Measured on the committed build, `-E landisk`, unmodified, under `step 3`:
  16 
  17     8c010000:  2102  mov.l r0,@r1 ; r1 = 0xf6000000     <- entry 0, indexed
  18     8c010002:  2542  mov.l r4,@r5 ; r5 = 0xf6000100     <- entry 1, indexed
  19     8c010004:  2762  mov.l r6,@r7 ; r7 = 0xf6000080     <- ASSOCIATIVE
  20     [ exception 0x140, pc=0x8c010004 vaddr=0x00000000 ]
  21     sh_exception(): exception 0x140 is not yet implemented.
  22       -> host process gone
  23 
  24 *** SURVIVAL IS NOT ENOUGH, AND NEITHER IS EXPEVT PLUS PC.  Six mutants were BUILT
  25 and measured against this row set. ***
  26 
  27     mutA  detection deleted                passes alive
  28     mutB  own arm -> general vector        passes alive
  29     mutC  own arm, pc + vbr only           passes alive, expevt, pc AND vbr
  30     mutD  n_hits > 2                       passes alive
  31     mutE  device raises RESET_MANUAL       passes alive, pc, vbr
  32     mutF  n_hits >= 1                      passes EVERY row on the trigger
  33 
  34 `expevt == 0x140 && pc == 0xa0000000` kills mutA, mutB, mutD and mutE, and is passed
  35 by mutC and mutF.  Two rows exist solely to kill those two:
  36 
  37   * `sr under FD` -- pre-sets SR to 0x40008000 (MD|FD, IMASK=0) before the trigger,
  38     so the reset transition's THIRD statement becomes observable.  From the
  39     reset-default SR that statement is a NO-OP (IMASK already 0xf, FD already clear),
  40     which is exactly why mutC -- an arm that sets pc and vbr and forgets it -- is
  41     invisible to every other row.  Figure 5.2 (`sh7750_hardware.txt:12228`) specifies
  42     SR.{MD,RB,BL,FD,IMASK} <- 11101111 for this transition.
  43   * `single hit` -- the identical program with entry 1 given a DIFFERENT VPN.  Nothing
  44     should fire.  It is the only row that sees mutF, which fires on one match.
  45 
  46 *** THE RIG IS LANDISK, NOT TESTSH, AND THAT IS FORCED. ***  landisk's PROM leaves
  47 `vbr = 0x8c000000` (`promemul/sh_ipl_g.c:55`), so `vbr == 0` after the fault is a REAL
  48 transition and mutB's `vbr + 0x100` is distinguishable.  Measured cold-start `vbr` on
  49 testsh is already `0x00000000`, which would make that row vacuous there.
  50 
  51 Two further facts worth carrying, both measured rather than assumed:
  52 
  53   * The exception flips `SR.RB`, so `r0-r7` are the other bank afterwards.  Anything
  54     read back across the fault uses `r8-r15`, which are unbanked.
  55   * `cpu_sh.c` USED TO rewrite ANY expevt to `EXPEVT_RESET_POWER` when `SR.BL` is set
  56     (a BL-set guest silently latched `0x000`, the multiple hit included).  #577 makes it
  57     `EXPEVT_RESET_MANUAL` with the multiple-hit code exempt; the BL rows at the end of
  58     this file pin both halves.
  59 """
  60 import os
  61 import pty
  62 import re
  63 import select
  64 import sys
  65 import time
  66 
  67 BIN = sys.argv[1]
  68 KERNEL = sys.argv[2]
  69 
  70 CODE = 0x8c010000
  71 UTLB_AA = 0xf6000000           # SH4_UTLB_AA, 16 MB window
  72 ENTRY0 = UTLB_AA + 0x000
  73 ENTRY1 = UTLB_AA + 0x100
  74 ASSOC = UTLB_AA + 0x080        # SH4_UTLB_A, the associative form
  75 VPN_A = 0x12345100             # VPN 0x12345000, ASID 0, V=1
  76 VPN_B = 0x22345100             # a DIFFERENT VPN -- the single-hit control
  77 
  78 MOV_L_R0_AT_R1 = 0x2102        # mov.l r0,@r1
  79 MOV_L_R4_AT_R5 = 0x2542        # mov.l r4,@r5
  80 MOV_L_R6_AT_R7 = 0x2762        # mov.l r6,@r7
  81 
  82 rows = []
  83 
  84 
  85 def row(name, got, want):
  86     ok = (got == want)
  87     rows.append(ok)
  88     print("%-14s %-24s %-24s %-10s %s"
  89           % (name, got, want, "#457", "ok" if ok else "FAIL"))
  90 
  91 
  92 def session(pre=(), entry1_vpn=VPN_A, settle=8.0, trigger=True, program=None, steps=None):
  93     """Install two UTLB entries then do the associative write. Returns (regs, died).
  94 
  95     `pre` runs before the trigger -- used to pre-set SR so the reset transition's
  96     SR update is observable.
  97     #577: `program` (a list of 16-bit words placed at CODE) and `steps` replace the
  98     three-store multiple-hit program for the BL rows; the default is that program.
  99     """
 100     pid, fd = pty.fork()
 101     if pid == 0:
 102         os.execv(BIN, [BIN, "-V", "-E", "landisk", "-M", "64", KERNEL])
 103         os._exit(127)
 104     buf = ""
 105 
 106     def rd(t):
 107         nonlocal buf
 108         end = time.time() + t
 109         while time.time() < end:
 110             r, _, _ = select.select([fd], [], [], 0.25)
 111             if not r:
 112                 continue
 113             try:
 114                 d = os.read(fd, 65536)
 115             except OSError:
 116                 return False
 117             if not d:
 118                 return False
 119             buf += d.decode("latin-1", "replace")
 120         return True
 121 
 122     alive = rd(settle)
 123     #  *** THE CONTROL MUST NOT RUN THE TRIGGER. ***  The first draft ran the three
 124     #  stores unconditionally, so the "does the session come up" control EXERCISED the
 125     #  defect and reported DEAD on the committed build -- a control failing for the
 126     #  very reason it exists to rule out.  Rule 4: did it fail for the reason under
 127     #  test?  It did not.
 128     if program is None:
 129         trig = ["r0=0x%08x" % VPN_A, "r1=0x%x" % ENTRY0,
 130                 "r4=0x%08x" % entry1_vpn, "r5=0x%x" % ENTRY1,
 131                 "r6=0x%08x" % VPN_A, "r7=0x%x" % ASSOC,
 132                 "put h 0x%x, 0x%04x" % (CODE, MOV_L_R0_AT_R1),
 133                 "put h 0x%x, 0x%04x" % (CODE + 2, MOV_L_R4_AT_R5),
 134                 "put h 0x%x, 0x%04x" % (CODE + 4, MOV_L_R6_AT_R7),
 135                 "pc=0x%x" % CODE, "step 3"]
 136     else:   # #577: an arbitrary short program; the caller seeds registers through `pre`
 137         trig = ["put h 0x%x, 0x%04x" % (CODE + 2 * i, w) for i, w in enumerate(program)]
 138         trig += ["pc=0x%x" % CODE, "step %d" % (steps if steps is not None else len(program))]
 139     cmds = list(pre) + ([] if not trigger else trig) + [
 140         #  `registers` does not exist as a command, and a bare dump would not show
 141         #  these anyway: cpu_sh.c prints expevt/vbr only under `coprocs & 2`.
 142         #  `print <name>` reads them through CPU_SETTINGS_ADD_REGISTER32.  Established
 143         #  by trying the candidates against a live session, not assumed.
 144         "print expevt", "print pc", "print vbr", "print sr"]
 145     for c in cmds:
 146         try:
 147             os.write(fd, (c + "\n").encode("latin-1"))
 148         except OSError:
 149             alive = False
 150             break
 151         if not rd(1.2):
 152             alive = False
 153             break
 154     try:
 155         os.write(fd, b"quit\n")
 156         time.sleep(0.2)
 157         os.kill(pid, 9)
 158         os.waitpid(pid, 0)
 159     except Exception:
 160         pass
 161     return buf, not alive
 162 
 163 
 164 def reg(t, name):
 165     """Read back one `print <name>`: the debugger echoes the command, then the value.
 166 
 167     Anchored to the ECHO rather than scanning for a bare hex word, because the
 168     transcript is full of addresses and the wrong one would be indistinguishable from
 169     the right one -- the same reason this project's verdict extractor anchors instead
 170     of grepping.
 171     """
 172     m = re.search(r"print\s+%s\s*\r?\n\s*0x([0-9a-f]+)" % re.escape(name), t)
 173     return ("0x%08x" % int(m.group(1), 16)) if m else "absent"
 174 
 175 
 176 #  ---- control: the session comes up at all ------------------------------------
 177 ctl, ctl_died = session(trigger=False)
 178 print("SH_TLBMULTI_CONTROL=%s" % ("DEAD" if ctl_died else "OK"))
 179 if ctl_died:
 180     print("SH_TLBMULTI_RESULT=0/0")
 181     sys.exit(0)
 182 
 183 #  ---- the trigger, at reset-default SR ----------------------------------------
 184 t, died = session()
 185 row("tlbm alive", "died" if died else "alive", "alive")
 186 row("tlbm expevt", reg(t, "expevt") if not died else "died", "0x00000140")
 187 row("tlbm pc", reg(t, "pc") if not died else "died", "0xa0000000")
 188 row("tlbm vbr", reg(t, "vbr") if not died else "died", "0x00000000")
 189 
 190 #  ---- the SR row: the ONLY row that sees a pc+vbr-only arm --------------------
 191 t2, died2 = session(pre=["sr=0x40008000"])
 192 row("tlbm sr", reg(t2, "sr") if not died2 else "died", "0x700000f0")
 193 
 194 #  ---- the single-hit control: the ONLY row that sees `n_hits >= 1` ------------
 195 #  A LIVENESS control too: it proves the three stores execute and the session
 196 #  survives them, so "died" on the rows above is the SECOND match and not the
 197 #  program.
 198 t3, died3 = session(entry1_vpn=VPN_B)
 199 row("tlbm single", "died" if died3 else reg(t3, "expevt"), "0x00000000")
 200 
 201 
 202 #  ---- #577: a general exception taken with SR.BL set is a MANUAL reset -----------
 203 #  sh7750_hardware.txt 5.5.3 (:12302-12304): with BL set, a general exception other than a
 204 #  user break performs a manual reset; EXPEVT is H'020 (:678-681).  Table 5.2 (:12006,
 205 #  :12010) lists the two TLB multiple-hit exceptions as reset-category in their own right,
 206 #  code H'140 (:12461), so the BL rule must not touch them.  HEAD's sh_exception() rewrote
 207 #  EVERY code to EXPEVT_RESET_POWER (H'000) when BL was set; #577 makes it EXPEVT_RESET_MANUAL
 208 #  with the multiple-hit code exempt.  Rows run under sr = MD|BL (0x500000f0, RB clear so the
 209 #  bank-0 seeds are the ones the program uses); `tlbm trapa' is the BL-CLEAR control that pins
 210 #  the general vector's own code.  Contract: TRAPA (H'160) and a misaligned load (H'0E0) are
 211 #  the two general codes driven; a re-introduction of the rewrite keyed to a code this table
 212 #  does not drive (a TLB miss, a reserved instruction) is clause-(e) disclosure.  The identity
 213 #  medium for this predicate round is the BL block DELETED: `tlbm bl trapa' and `tlbm bl ldmis'
 214 #  then read their own codes (red); `tlbm bl mhit' reads H'140 either way and cannot carry it.
 215 #  Names stay at 13 characters or fewer: row() prints `%-14s' and the gate anchors `^$v  .*ok$'
 216 #  with TWO spaces (Grok, pass 1 -- the padded-column trap).
 217 SR_MD_BL = 0x500000f0
 218 SR_MD = 0x400000f0
 219 TRAPA_1 = 0xc301            # trapa #1  : 1100 0011 0000 0001
 220 MOV_L_AT_R1_R2 = 0x6212     # mov.l @r1,r2 : 0110 0010 0001 0010
 221 t5, died5 = session(pre=["sr=0x%08x" % SR_MD_BL], program=[TRAPA_1], steps=1)
 222 row("tlbm bl trapa", "died" if died5 else reg(t5, "expevt"), "0x00000020")
 223 t6, died6 = session(pre=["sr=0x%08x" % SR_MD_BL])
 224 row("tlbm bl mhit", "died" if died6 else reg(t6, "expevt"), "0x00000140")
 225 t7, died7 = session(pre=["sr=0x%08x" % SR_MD_BL, "r1=0x%08x" % (CODE + 1)], program=[MOV_L_AT_R1_R2], steps=1)
 226 row("tlbm bl ldmis", "died" if died7 else reg(t7, "expevt"), "0x00000020")
 227 t8, died8 = session(pre=["sr=0x%08x" % SR_MD], program=[TRAPA_1], steps=1)
 228 row("tlbm trapa", "died" if died8 else reg(t8, "expevt"), "0x00000160")
 229 
 230 print("SH_TLBMULTI_RESULT=%d/%d" % (sum(1 for r in rows if r), len(rows)))
# `#577` (2026-11-02) -- `shblreset`: a SuperH general exception taken with SR.BL set stored the power-on reset code, and clobbered the TLB multiple-hit code

**The defect.**  `src/cpus/cpu_sh.c`, `sh_exception()` (HEAD `987cb596` :910-918): when SR.BL was already set the block printed its
`fatal()` and then executed `expevt = EXPEVT_RESET_POWER;` for EVERY exception code, under a `/* TODO */`.  The SH7750 manual
(`_scratchpad/sh7750_hardware.txt`) says a general exception other than a user break taken with BL set performs a MANUAL reset -- 5.5.3
`:12302-12304`, 5.6.1 (2) `:12376` -- and "Exception code H'020 is set in EXPEVT" (`:12383-12384`; 5.7.2.a `:13164-13166` repeats it as
H'0000 0020), not the power-on code H'000; and the two TLB multiple-hit exceptions are reset-category in their own right (Table 5.2
`:12006`, `:12010`) with their own code H'140 (`:12461` instruction side, `:12499` data side), which the block overwrote too -- so the
`#457` guest-distinguishability comment at `:985-989` ("a multiple hit can be told from a power-on (0x000) or a manual reset (0x020)")
was false under BL.  Guest-visible consequence: a kernel's reset handler dispatching on EXPEVT read 0x000 for a manual reset and for a
multiple hit alike.  Upstream residue (the TODO is the 0.7.0 import's).  WRONG-RESULT, MED; no host failure path (`fatal()` only prints,
`debugmsg.c:384-391`).  Two carriers in the bug file: the id entry `OUTSTANDING_BUGS.md:24063` and the prose row `:8238`.

**The witness (rung 3).**  `regress/artifacts/shblreset/witness_20261102/sh_blreset_witness.py` on the unmodified in-tree `-E landisk`
(the rig kernel loaded for construction only), the cold debugger presetting `sr` (MD|BL = 0x500000f0, RB clear) and `pc`, the guest
executing `trapa #1` (0xc301) or the TLB multiple-hit raiser's path, `expevt`/`pc` read back through the debugger.  On a fresh clone of
HEAD built in WSL (`/tmp/gxdivw`, binary newer than source): `witness_head.out` RESULT=2/4 -- both failures read H'000 against the wanted
H'020 and H'140 -- with the liveness control (`bl trapa pc` 0xa0000000, the reset vector) and the BL-clear control (`nobl trapa expevt`
0x160) green.  The same script on the fixed clone (`/tmp/gxfix577`, 17:47): `witness_fixed.out` RESULT=4/4.

**The fix.**  In the BL block, `expevt = EXPEVT_RESET_POWER;` becomes `if (expevt != EXPEVT_RESET_TLB_MULTI_HIT) expevt =
EXPEVT_RESET_MANUAL;`, and the TODO comment becomes a twelve-line `#577` comment carrying the manual citations above, the reason the
multiple-hit code is exempt, why a user break never reaches the block (the UBC suppresses it under BL, `:41448-41452`, and
`EXPEVT_BREAK` has no raiser in this tree -- `sh4_exception.h:73` is its only occurrence), and why an interrupt cannot latch a code here
(`cpu_dyntrans.c:247` delivers none while BL is set; the intevt path at `:945-947` never stores EXPEVT for an interrupt).  Nothing else
in `sh_exception()` changes: the `fatal()` stays (its flood is `floodclass`, not this round's), the common tail and the shared reset arm
(`:1015-1021`) are untouched.  Option set: IMPLEMENT the manual's rule -- the arm already existed and only its constant was wrong; there
is nothing to DECLINE or FAULT (the exception is legal and the manual says exactly what happens), and DELETE would leave the guest's own
code in EXPEVT where the architecture mandates H'020.  Diff: `src/cpus/cpu_sh.c` +14 -5 (`killtable_20261102/product.diff`, the
shipping text; `witness_20261102/product.diff` and its `apply_fix577.py` carry the pre-pass-1 wording of the SAME code -- comment-only,
and both builds share the binary md5 `b7b0d0b5f5ae` at 17:47 and 18:11), byte-identical in `GXEMUL-SEC` and `est/`.  Every caller of
`sh_exception()` at HEAD was enumerated at pass 2 (Fable; `git grep`): no caller passes H'000 or H'020 as an exception, so the exempt set
is exactly {H'140} and every value the fix stores has an arm in the switch -- the fix opens no path to the `default: ... exit(1)` at
`:1083-1085`.

**The detector.**  `regress/sh_tlbmulti_probe.py`: `session()` gains `program=`/`steps=` (a short guest program run under a preset `sr`),
and four rows are appended -- `tlbm bl trapa` (sr 0x500000f0, `trapa #1`, want 0x00000020), `tlbm bl mhit` (the multiple hit under BL,
want 0x00000140), `tlbm bl ldmis` (`mov.l @r1,r2` = 0x6212 with r1 odd under BL: the misaligned-load code H'0E0 is rewritten, want
0x00000020) and `tlbm trapa` (sr 0x400000f0, BL clear, want 0x00000160: the control that pins the general vector's own code and, measured
post-table, the sole carrier of the guard-side class).  Names stay at 13 characters or fewer (`row()` prints `%-14s`, the gate anchors
`^$v  .*ok$` with two spaces: the padded-column trap, Grok pass 1).  The docstring's "rewrites ANY expevt" note is historicised.
Contract (the probe's `#577` comment, final text after three post-table comment-only edits logged in `ASRUN_NOTE.txt`): TRAPA (H'160)
and a misaligned load (H'0E0) are the two general codes driven; any edit that moves a code between the rewritten set and the exempt set
ONLY at a code this table does not drive -- H'040-H'0C0, H'100, H'120, H'180, H'1A0, H'800, H'820 -- in either direction is clause-(e)
disclosure; the identity medium is the REWRITE deleted (the guard and its `fatal()` stay), carried by `tlbm bl trapa` and `tlbm bl ldmis`;
`tlbm bl mhit` reads H'140 either way and cannot carry it.  `regress/gate_sh_rounding.sh`: `sh_tlbmulti rows run` 6 -> 10 (EQUALITY),
the four names in the per-row loop.

**The pre-table check and the kill table** (`regress/artifacts/shblreset/killtable_20261102/`; scratch clones only, a `.MUTANT` sentinel
per mutant; each `<leg>.raw` names its binary, md5, freshness and -- for the post-table legs -- the instrument's md5):

    base_head (HEAD)                                              7/10   bl trapa, bl mhit, bl ldmis all 0x000
    fixed                                                        10/10
    M_b        the power-on store reinstated verbatim (b)         7/10   the same three (binary md5 == HEAD's)
    M_c        the rewrite deleted, guard and fatal() kept (c)    8/10   bl trapa 0x160, bl ldmis 0x0e0
    M_noex     exemption removed (d, body)                        9/10   bl mhit 0x020
    M_wrongex  exemption on TRAPA instead of the multiple hit     8/10   bl trapa 0x160, bl mhit 0x020
    M_lt100    exemption widened to every code below 0x100        8/10   bl mhit 0x020, bl ldmis 0x0e0  (predicted 9/10; corrected)
    M_trapaonly the rewrite keyed to TRAPA only (e)               9/10   bl ldmis 0x0e0
