 12298 Section 5 Exceptions
 12299 
 12300 5.5.3 Exception Requests and BL Bit
 12301 When the BL bit in SR is 0, general exception and interrupts are accepted.
 12302 When the BL bit in SR is 1 and a general exception other than a user break is generated, the CPU's
 12303 internal registers and the registers of the other modules are set to their states following a manual
 12304 reset, and the CPU branches to the same address as in a reset (H'A000 0000). For the operation in
 12305 the event of a user break, see section 20, User Break Controller (UBC).
 12306 If an ordinary interrupt occurs, the interrupt request is held pending and is accepted after the BL
 12307 bit has been cleared to 0 by software. If a nonmaskable interrupt (NMI) occurs, it can be held
 12308 pending or accepted according to the setting made by software.
 12309 Thus, normally, SPC and SSR are saved and then the BL bit in SR is cleared to 0, to enable
 12310 multiple exception state acceptance.
 12372 (2) Manual Reset
 12373 
 12374 � Sources:
 12375      SCK2 pin low level and RESET pin low level
 12376      When a general exception other than a user break occurs while the BL bit is set to 1 in SR
 12377      When the watchdog timer overflows while the WT/IT bit and RSTS bit are both set to 1 in
 12378         WTCSR. For details, see section 10, Clock Oscillation Circuits.
 12379 
 12380 � Transition address: H'A000 0000
 12381 � Transition operations:
 12382 
 12383     Exception code H'020 is set in EXPEVT, initialization of VBR and SR is performed, and a
 12384     branch is made to PC = H'A000 0000.
 12385     In the initialization processing, the VBR register is set to H'0000 0000, and in SR, the MD,
 12386     RB, and BL bits are set to 1, the FD bit is cleared to 0, and the interrupt mask bits (IMASK)
 12387     are set to B'1111.
 12388     CPU and on-chip peripheral module initialization is performed. For details, see the register
 12389     descriptions in the relevant sections.
 12390 
 12391    Manual_reset()
 12392    {
 12393 
 12394          EXPEVT = H'00000020;
 12395          VBR = H'00000000;
 12396          SR.MD = 1;
 12397          SR.RB = 1;
 12398          SR.BL = 1;
 12399          SR.IMASK = B'1111;
 12400          SR.FD = 0;
 12401          Initialize_CPU();
 12402          Initialize_Module(Manual);
 12403          PC = H'A0000000;
 12404    }
